PRE-ALPHA
---------
This core is pre-alpha. It is not fit for everyday use or packaging.

This software is not distributable in binary form due to license conflicts.

Gngeo JG
--------
Gngeo JG is an emulator for the Neo Geo.

This is a fork of Gngeo 0.8.1 with many things rewritten or replaced. The CPUs
were entirely replaced, as was the YM2610 emulation code, which is now a C
translation of YMFM (the same code used in MAME). Timing was also completely
rewritten, and the standalone interface code was removed.

This repository lives at https://gitlab.com/jgemu/gngeo

Compiling
---------
Make sure you have The Jolly Good API's header files installed. If you did
not install them, you will be required to include their path in CFLAGS.

Options:
  USE_VENDORED_SPEEXDSP - Set to a non-zero value to use vendored SpeexDSP.

Linux:
  make

macOS:
  make

BSD:
  gmake

Windows (MSYS2):
  make

The build will be output to "gngeo/". This directory may be used as is
locally by copying it to your local "cores" directory, or may be installed
system-wide using the "install" target specified in the Makefile.

